Mr. Vijayakumar has published scholarly articles in IEEE Flagship Conferences and Book Chapters in the field of Artificial Intelligence (AI) applications on High-Performance Computing, and Quantum Computing
Mr. Vijayakumar's consistent dedication to scholarly publishing since 2012 is evident through his remarkable record and significant contributions in AI, High-Performance Computing, and Quantum Computing. He has published 4 research papers, including 3 as the first author in prestigious IEEE conference proceedings such as IEEE Quantum Week-QCE (2022), IEEE TENCON (2019), and IEEE Cloud (2012). These publications have garnered widespread recognition, underscoring the exceptional quality and impact of his work. In addition to his conference papers, Mr. Vijayakumar's sole-authored paper has been accepted for publication in IEEE TENSYMP (2023), further solidifying his expertise and reputation in his research domain. The consistent acceptance of his papers in flagship IEEE conferences globally underscores his unwavering commitment to producing high-quality research. 
Mr. Vijayakumar's contributions extend beyond conference papers to include patent filings. After the publication of his 4 research papers, 3 of them were filed as patents in the India patent office. Notably, Mr. Vijayakumar is listed as the first inventor in 2 of these cases, further highlighting his involvement and contribution to these inventions. One of these patents has already been granted, emphasizing the practical significance and value of his work. This accomplishment not only emphasizes the value of his research but also solidifies his expertise and reputation as inventor within the field. Furthermore, his research papers have garnered 30 citations from esteemed academic and industry research institutions, indicating the acclaim and appreciation his work has garnered from the scholarly community. [Exhibit – 24]
Furthermore, he has been selected as the sole author for 2 book chapters to be published by esteemed publishers, CRC Press and Elsevier, in 2023 [Exhibit – 25]. This distinction serves as a significant validation of the importance and excellence of his research, strengthening his reputation in the academic community. Mr. Vijayakumar's expertise in AI, High-Performance Computing, and Quantum Computing is widely recognized by prestigious conferences and esteemed publishers. His consistent authorship commitment is clearly reflected in his dedication to scholarly publishing, as demonstrated by his research papers, conference publications, patent filling & grants and upcoming book chapters. His continuous efforts to bridge the gap between theoretical advancements and real-world applications showcase his unwavering commitment to high-quality research and contributes to the development of intellectual property.

